L205:  | $$\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}(\mathcal{G}_{t})\|^{2}\right]\leq\frac{2(\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}(\mathcal{G}_{0})-\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}^{*})}{T\eta_{\phi}}+2\beta\delta^{2}+O\left(\frac{d_{\max}D_{\max}L}{T}\right),$$  |  | (23)
L206: 
L207: where $\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}^{*}$ is the global minimum, and the expectation is over data stochasticity and shifts.
L208: Proof. Consider the meta-update: $\phi_{t+1}=\phi_{t}-\eta_{\phi}\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}+m_{t+1}$, with $m_{t+1}=\beta m_{t}+(1-\beta)\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}$. By $\beta$-smoothness,
L209: 
L210:  | $$\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}(\phi_{t+1})\leq\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}(\phi_{t})+\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}^{\top}(\phi_{t+1}-\phi_{t})+\frac{\beta}{2}\|\phi_{t+1}-\phi_{t}\|^{2}.$$  |  | (24)
L211: 
L212: Substituting the update and taking expectations,
L213:  | $$\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}(\phi_{t+1})]\leq\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}(\phi_{t})]-\eta_{\phi}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}\|^{2}]+\frac{\beta\eta_{\phi}^{2}}{2}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}\|^{2}]+\beta\delta^{2},$$  |  | (25)
L214: 
L215: accounting for shift-induced variance bounded by $\delta^{2}$. Rearranging and summing over $t=1$ to $T$,
L216:  | $$\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}[\|\nabla\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}(\phi_{t})\|^{2}]\leq\frac{2(\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}(\phi_{0})-\mathcal{L}_{\text{meta}}^{*})}{\eta_{\phi}(1-\beta\eta_{\phi})}+2T\beta\delta^{2}.$$  |  | (26)
L217: The additional $O(d_{\max}D_{\max}L/T)$ term arises from propagating gradients through the DAG, with depth bounded by $D_{\max}$ and branching by $d_{\max}$. Dividing by $T$ yields the result. For structural updates (level addition/pruning), the regret is sublinear as adaptations occur at rate $O(\sqrt{T}\delta)$, ensuring overall convergence.
L218: This theorem demonstrates that DNH achieves $O(1/T+\delta^{2})$ average gradient norm, improving over static NL’s $O(\delta)$ divergence in shifting environments [cite36†4 ].
