L1206@P18: Run Time (minutes)
L1207@P18: Figure 4. The relation between runtime for Rogue One and the number of entities of the datasets. Pearson correlation ρ = 0.949.
L1208@P18: C. Runtime
L1209@P18: The runtime is mainly driven by the training of XGBoost models during the testing phase, both by the Tester Agent and for
L1210@P18: acquiring evaluation metrics. The time complexity of training the XGBoost algorithm can be approximated to O(T · n · p),
L1211@P18: where T is the number of trees, n is the number of entries, and p is the number of attributes. T does remain constant, while
L1212@P18: d varies significantly less than n, thus for our tasks, n is the dominant factor of XGBoost time complexity, hence it can be
L1213@P18: expressed as O(n). This explains the observations in Figure 4, showing that Rogue One’s runtime correlates strongly with
L1214@P18: the number of entities n in the datasets, thus hinting towards a linear time complexity of O(n) for Rogue One.
